  "readme": "# Coordinate shell sources: completed local replay evidence\n\nThis initial delivery records the completed authenticated fresh-ZIP replay for\n`HDBLAST_COORDINATE_SHELL_SOURCES_20261015`. Its immutable source contains 55\napproved files; the matching ZIP contains those files and the manifest, for\n56 members. The complete source manifest and ZIP were authenticated against\nthe separate source-freeze receipt before scientific execution.\n\nThe actual replay completed 74 fresh processes across normal and optimized\nPython: 8 positive processes and 66 external mathematical/input corruptions\nrejected for their exact named reasons. The accepted roster has 105 named\npositive groups in each mode and zero embedded controls. The four programs in\neach mode are the primary generator and the independent Astra, Sol and\nfull-source/scope checkers. Counts and names are derived from the frozen\n`REPLAY_ROSTER.json`; the generator contributes zero enumerated check groups.\nAll 150 retained replay artifacts, including complete JSON results, full CSV\noutputs and process diagnostics, are preserved under `fresh-replay/`. Every\nconfigured output and its actual bytes were rechecked by the replay recorder.\nDisposable executable workspaces and raw literature responses are excluded.\n\nA separate completed-replay audit rechecked all 74 processes and 150 retained\nartifacts, the eight complete JSON goldens and two CSV outputs, and all 66 exact\ncontrol diagnostics without rerunning the scientific programs. Its audit source\nrecords the original local evidence layout; disposable process copies are not\npackaged.\n\nThe accompanying independent acceptance, frozen-source and completed-replay\nreviews are separate internal evidence. Their check inventories are not added to the four-program\nscientific replay roster. Source assembly, public/private path and exact-body\nexclusion checks, root approval, tool provenance, synthetic gate tests and\nindependent helper-review corrections are retained with their actual pins.\nPreparation-only records describe their own earlier stage and do not establish\nlater execution or remote publication facts. The two proposal configurations\nexplicitly hashed by the root prefreeze approval are retained as historical\nreview inputs; the separate approved configurations define the actual source\nand site integration. The input preparation script is a\nrecord of the local public-blob capture workflow; immutable public source URLs\nand final input-byte identities are retained in the source capsule. The\nfresh-referee audit source also records the original audit layout, including\nduplicate optimized-generator report/CSV paths. Those duplicate bodies are not\npackaged here; their bytes match the canonical optimized report and CSV in the\nsource capsule. These supporting audit programs remain outside its four-program\nfresh replay.\n\nThe calculation encloses the continuous metric boundary trace and its\nproper-time derivative and the complete one-copy coordinate scalar and\nisotropic Israel source coefficients over 4353 cells. It includes their\nscalar degree-0/2/4 projections, norms and central/tail sign certificates,\nand the degree-4 reduced Robin forcing norm. The source notes specify the\ncoordinate representative, derivative Taylor convention and retained analytic\nhypotheses. The degree-2 Robin row is algebraic only. The complete quantitative\nU2 response, a finite-amplitude nonlinear remainder, an observational scale\nand a cosmological-origin inference remain unavailable. Internal arithmetic\nand AI reviews do not replace external peer review or certify the analytic\nPDE hypotheses.\n\nLocal installation preserved all 44 existing workflows and added the dedicated\n45th replay workflow. The nine summaries and two figure assets were integrated\nand checked against their actual immutable baselines and source figure bytes;\nall other existing projects were preserved. These are local checks.\nAt this initial delivery stage, remote PR checks, merges, CI, deployments and\nlive readbacks are pending. Completed remote facts will be added separately\nwithout changing the initial delivery bytes. No new Zenodo version or APS\nsubmission is part of this checkpoint.\n",
